# Normalize line endings in the repository.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows, where core.autocrlf=true was checking Go
# sources out with CRLF. gofmt requires LF, so `gofmt -l .` reported every such
# file as unformatted even when its content was already correct, which made the
# formatting gate useless. Pinning eol=lf keeps working copies LF on all
# platforms so gofmt stays authoritative.

# Default: let Git detect text and normalize to LF in the index.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Go toolchain files must be LF.
*.go    text eol=lf
go.mod  text eol=lf
go.sum  text eol=lf

# Web assets and content served or parsed by the app.
*.html  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

# Shell scripts break if checked out with CRLF.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf

# Binary content Git must not touch.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
